| Change | Why |
|---|---|
| Removed `import java.util.Vector` | Dead import, never used. |
| `Stack` → `ArrayDeque` (`Deque`) | `Stack` is a legacy synchronized class; `ArrayDeque` is the recommended stack and is faster. |
| If-chain → `Map` of closing→opening pairs | Removes the repetitive three-way `peek`/compare logic; the matching rule now lives in one data structure. |
| `peek()`+`pop()` → single `pop()` compare | One operation instead of two. |
| `println(cond ? "true" : "false")` → `println(isBalanced(s))` | `println` already formats a boolean. |

Behavior is unchanged — same results for matched, mismatched, and unbalanced inputs.

